# UST G3AP Structural SCC Minor Factorization Lemma v1

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_STRUCTURAL_LINEAR_ALGEBRA_LEMMA`

This lemma is purely finite linear algebra. It does not assert that the G3AP
minor exists or that any emitted factor is nonsingular; those are separate
machine-checked premises.

## Lemma

Let `A` be an `n x n` matrix over a field and let `mu` be a perfect matching
of its bipartite nonzero graph. Permute the columns so that column `mu(i)` is
paired with row `i`. Define the directed matched graph on the row indices by

```text
i -> j  exactly when  A[i, mu(j)] != 0.
```

Let `C_1, ..., C_r` be its strongly connected components. A topological order
of the condensation DAG simultaneously permutes the matched rows and columns
so that `A` is block triangular, with diagonal blocks

```text
A[C_k, mu(C_k)].
```

Consequently,

```text
det(A) = sign * product_k det(A[C_k, mu(C_k)]).
```

In particular, `A` is nonsingular if and only if every diagonal SCC block is
nonsingular. One SCC may be checked separately from the direct sum of all
remaining SCCs: the latter induced submatrix is itself block triangular and
has determinant equal, up to sign, to the product of the remaining diagonal
blocks.

## Proof

Contract every matched row-column pair to one vertex. Every nonzero matrix
entry becomes a directed edge in the matched graph. Condensing strongly
connected components gives a DAG. In a topological ordering of that DAG, an
entry can occur only on a diagonal SCC block or on one permitted side of the
block diagonal. Thus the permuted matrix is block triangular. The determinant
formula for a block-triangular matrix gives the displayed product. The final
equivalence follows because a product in a field is nonzero exactly when every
factor is nonzero.

## G3AP use contract

For a G3AP closure packet to invoke this lemma, it must bind all of the
following:

1. the exact selected square minor;
2. a perfect matching of all `39,725` rows and columns;
3. the SCC decomposition derived from that same matching and nonzero graph;
4. exact factor matrices emitted from the matched row and column subsets;
5. independent exact ranks equal to the dimensions of every retained factor,
   or of a coarsening whose diagonal factors partition all SCCs.

Structural nonsingularity alone is not numerical nonsingularity. The matching
and SCC calculation therefore provide only the factorization; exact LinBox and
Givaro arithmetic must still prove the factor ranks.
